<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ONE row of the latest-messages widget, served by RecentMailWidgetService.

    Every text here is set at runtime and NONE is set in this file: what a row may say is
    RecentMailWidgetContent's decision, taken from the notification-content setting and the app
    lock, and a literal left in this layout would be a line the launcher draws before that rule ever
    runs. ⛔ Nothing here reads a database column either — the factory hands over strings that are
    already decided.

    ⛔ THE ROOT CARRIES AN ID because that is what a tap is attached to (setOnClickFillInIntent in
    RecentMailWidgetService): given to a child instead, only that child would open the message and
    the rest of the row would swallow the touch.

    Same closed list of views as the cell itself: LinearLayout, TextView, ImageView.

    ⛔ READ AND UNREAD ARE TOLD APART BY WEIGHT, AND BY NOTHING ELSE — there is no unread dot on
    this row, and re-adding one would say the same thing twice. The message list inside the app
    settled that long ago (EmailListItem: "Unread is shown by weight (bold) rather than a status
    dot"), and a home-screen cell that marks unread differently from the list it opens is the app
    contradicting itself on the one piece of state a row carries. The weight is set at runtime, as
    a StyleSpan inside the text (RecentMailWidgetService.weighted): RemoteViews has no way to set a
    typeface on a TextView.

    TWO IMAGEVIEWS HOLD THE COLUMN, and both are VISIBLE or INVISIBLE, never GONE. The badge comes
    first, the account dot second. The list interleaves several accounts by date, so rows that wear
    no dot (one account only, or an account left on the picker's "auto" position) sit beside rows
    that do; and rows carry no badge at all under the app lock or at the NONE position of the
    notification-content setting. A GONE view in either place would shift that row's sender left
    against its neighbours, for no reason the reader can see.

    ⛔ NEITHER IS NAMED OUT LOUD: importantForAccessibility="no" and no contentDescription on both.
    Reading the account's name is the naming the app lock exists to prevent, and speaking the
    initial is the same leak one letter at a time — on a locked screen the badge is not drawn, and
    a talkback string would have said aloud what the pixels deliberately do not.

    ⛔ NO android:src ON THE BADGE. It is a Bitmap posted at runtime (RecentMailWidgetService →
    WidgetMonogram), painted in the tones read beside the rows; a compile-time drawable here would
    be a colour this layout chose, on rows the palette has not answered for yet.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widget_recent_row_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:gravity="center_vertical"
    android:orientation="horizontal"
    android:paddingTop="6dp"
    android:paddingBottom="6dp">

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/widget_recent_row_monogram"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/widget_recent_monogram"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/widget_recent_monogram"
        android:layout_marginEnd="8dp"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no" />

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/widget_recent_row_account"
        android:layout_width="8dp"
        android:layout_height="8dp"
        android:layout_marginEnd="8dp"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:src="@drawable/widget_recent_account_dot" />

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="0dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_recent_row_primary"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_row_primary"
            android:textSize="14sp" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_recent_row_secondary"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textColor="@color/widget_unread_label"
            android:textSize="12sp" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_recent_row_date"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="8dp"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_unread_label"
        android:textSize="12sp" />
</LinearLayout>
